{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ydYr4Hmmus4LA1iZqgQQy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n2\t\n3\t## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n4\t\n5\t> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n6\t> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n7\t> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n8\t> Safari and Chrome.\n9\t\n10\tReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\n11\tweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\n12\tgotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n13\t\n14\t## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n15\t\n16\t> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n17\t> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n18\t> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n19\t> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n20\t> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n21\t\n22\tChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n23\t\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n24\t`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\n25\tlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\n26\tbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\n27\tsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\n28\tIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\n29\tathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n30\t`connect-attempt.log`).\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be23feb-15d3-44ab-a69c-e5413bcf79e2","uuid":"4173a549-1280-447b-b759-0fd56ca309db","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:11.490Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-xoUxIO/logs/support-tickets.md","content":"# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n\n## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n\n> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n> Safari and Chrome.\n\nReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\nweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\ngotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n\n## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n\n> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n\nChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\nlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\nbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\nsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\nIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\nathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n`connect-attempt.log`).\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018ydYr4Hmmus4LA1iZqgQQy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
