{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHoEuZNWwB5CDwQMnEuHtn","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu OAuth authorize scope parameter ACTIVITY:READ CALENDAR:WRITE WELLNESS:READ API documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"},{\"title\":\"Überauth intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-integration-cookbook/80090\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"},{\"title\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth support\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759/35\"},{\"title\":\"intervals icu tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools\"},{\"title\":\"open api\",\"url\":\"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/\"},{\"title\":\"intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=14\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the intervals.icu OAuth documentation, which confirms the scope format you asked about, though not the exact scope strings in your query.\n\n- **Format:** Scopes are specified as READ or WRITE, with commas separating multiple scopes. The docs give the example ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE.\n- **Authorization request:** You send the user to the authorize endpoint with a client ID, redirect URI, scope, and optional state. Intervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which scopes to grant the application.\n- **Scope meanings:** ACTIVITY covers completed activities, WELLNESS covers items like weight and resting HR, and CALENDAR covers planned workouts. Other scopes include CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS (per the scope list in the forum thread).\n- **Endpoint scope requirements:** The Integration Cookbook says the bulk wellness upload endpoint requires WELLNESS:WRITE scope, and the list wellness endpoint requires WELLNESS:READ scope. For activities, uploading requires the ACTIVITY:WRITE scope.\n- **Token response:** The token exchange returns the granted scopes, so you can check what the user actually approved.\n\nI did not find a documented scope string that matches your query exactly. The forum mentions an ATHLETES scope, found in the Swagger docs, but it reportedly did not work for one developer. I also found no source confirming that CALENDAR:WRITE is an exact valid string beyond the general CALENDAR scope description. The official API docs at intervals.icu/api-docs.html would be the place to confirm it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be23feb-15d3-44ab-a69c-e5413bcf79e2","uuid":"152b5f27-60af-4e35-8714-466a2f6a1704","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:36.699Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu OAuth authorize scope parameter ACTIVITY:READ CALENDAR:WRITE WELLNESS:READ API documentation","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_0151XpXyXSYZo3tgwqK2JFRA","content":[{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},{"title":"Überauth intervals.icu","url":"https://readme.hex.pm/ueberauth_intervals_icu/0.1.0"},{"title":"Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090.md"},{"title":"Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090"},{"title":"Intervals.icu OAuth support","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759/35"},{"title":"intervals icu tools","url":"https://github.com/kuranov/intervals-icu-tools"},{"title":"open api","url":"https://www.intervals.icu/features/open-api/"},{"title":"intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=14"}]},"The search turned up the intervals.icu OAuth documentation, which confirms the scope format you asked about, though not the exact scope strings in your query.\n\n- **Format:** Scopes are specified as READ or WRITE, with commas separating multiple scopes. The docs give the example ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE.\n- **Authorization request:** You send the user to the authorize endpoint with a client ID, redirect URI, scope, and optional state. Intervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which scopes to grant the application.\n- **Scope meanings:** ACTIVITY covers completed activities, WELLNESS covers items like weight and resting HR, and CALENDAR covers planned workouts. Other scopes include CHATS, LIBRARY, and SETTINGS (per the scope list in the forum thread).\n- **Endpoint scope requirements:** The Integration Cookbook says the bulk wellness upload endpoint requires WELLNESS:WRITE scope, and the list wellness endpoint requires WELLNESS:READ scope. For activities, uploading requires the ACTIVITY:WRITE scope.\n- **Token response:** The token exchange returns the granted scopes, so you can check what the user actually approved.\n\nI did not find a documented scope string that matches your query exactly. The forum mentions an ATHLETES scope, found in the Swagger docs, but it reportedly did not work for one developer. I also found no source confirming that CALENDAR:WRITE is an exact valid string beyond the general CALENDAR scope description. The official API docs at intervals.icu/api-docs.html would be the place to confirm it."],"durationSecon