{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBSQMz24uThBJhrkWK5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014mz3w6ccJ1eYe3kmjvcZMn","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759","prompt":"Summarize the OAuth details: authorize URL params, valid scope names (exact strings, incl. CALENDAR), whether refresh tokens are issued, token expiry / expires_in, token response fields, redirect_uri rules, and any reported invalid_request errors and their causes."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5152,"cache_read_input_tokens":30383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5152},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be23feb-15d3-44ab-a69c-e5413bcf79e2","uuid":"3aed0f69-3afa-4786-9c98-41a90df2bb7a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:39.462Z","request_id":"req_011CgSBSPsi3ueryTDmxhyCP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014mz3w6ccJ1eYe3kmjvcZMn":{"url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759","prompt":"Summarize the OAuth details: authorize URL params, valid scope names (exact strings, incl. CALENDAR), whether refresh tokens are issued, token expiry / expires_in, token response fields, redirect_uri rules, and any reported invalid_request errors and their causes."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014mz3w6ccJ1eYe3kmjvcZMn","type":"tool_result","content":"**Authorize URL:** Send users to `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize` with these parameters:\n- `client_id` (required)\n- `redirect_uri` (required)\n- `scope` (required)\n- `state` (optional, returned unchanged)\n- `code_challenge` and `code_challenge_method=S256` (optional, for PKCE)\n\n**Scopes:** Use these exact names, each with `:READ` or `:WRITE` (WRITE implies READ), separated by commas, e.g. `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE`.\n- `ACTIVITY`: completed activities\n- `WELLNESS`: weight, resting HR, etc.\n- `CALENDAR`: planned workouts\n- `CHATS`: chats, groups, and messages\n- `LIBRARY`: workout library\n- `SETTINGS`: athlete settings\n\n**Token exchange:** POST to `https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token` with `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`. The code must be exchanged within 2 minutes. With PKCE, include `code_verifier`. Public clients using PKCE can omit `client_secret`.\n\n**Token response fields:** `token_type`, `access_token`, `scope`, and `athlete` (with `id` and `name`). No `expires_in` field is documented.\n\n**Refresh tokens:** None are issued. The page says Intervals.icu \"doesn’t use refresh tokens, only access tokens.\"\n\n**Expiry:** The page does not document a token lifetime. A 2022 forum reply describes the token as effectively one-time, with a new login replacing the old token, but this is anecdotal. Another user reported 403 errors after a few hours, and no official answer appears in the thread. David also said a new token is generated on each authorization and replaces any existing one.\n\n**Redirect URI rules:**\n- Redirect URIs must be registered on the app's management page.\n- For registered `http://localhost` or `http://127.0.0.1` URIs, the port is ignored.\n- Public clients do not get the automatic localhost exception, so they must register the exact localhost URIs they use.\n\n**Other requirements:**\n- The app must be approved before the OAuth flow works. Until then it shows as \"Pending.\"\n- Declined consent returns `error=access_denied` to the redirect URI.\n- PKCE mismatches are rejected: a verifier without a challenge, or a challenge without a verifier.\n- Once \"Require PKCE\" is enabled, authorizations without a challenge are rejected.\n- To revoke a token, send a DELETE to `https://intervals.icu/api/v1/disconnect-app` with a Bearer header. This stops webhook delivery.\n\n**Reported invalid_request errors:** The page does not mention any `invalid_request` error. The only errors reported are `access_denied` (user declined) and a 403 reported by one developer, with no confirmed cause. The documented rejections above (PKCE mismatches and missing `client_secret`) are the closest to request-validation failures."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2be23feb-15d3-44ab-a69c-e5413bcf79e2","uuid":"86b09e23-628d-41f0-b2a7-6ddd697dd71b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:21:49.095Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":66890,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Authorize URL:** Send users to `https://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize` with these parameters:\n- `client_id` (required)\n- `redirect_uri` (required)\n- `scope` (required)\n- `state` (optional, returned unchanged)\n- `code_challenge` and `code_challenge_method=S256` (optional, for PKCE)\n\n**Scopes:** Use these exact names, each with `:READ` or `:WRITE` (WRITE implies READ), separated by commas, e.g. `ACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE`.\n- `ACTIVITY`: completed activities\n- `WELLNESS`: weight, resting HR, etc.\n- `CALENDAR`: planned workouts\n- `CHATS`: chats, groups, and messages\n- `LIBRARY`: workout library\n- `SETTINGS`: athlete settings\n\n**Token exchange:** POST to `https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token` with `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code`. The code must be exchanged within 2 minutes. With PKCE, include `code_verifier`. Public clients using PKCE can omit `client_secret`.\n\n**Token response fields:** `token_type`, `access_token`, `scope`, and `athlete` (with `id` and `name`). No `expires_in` field is documented.\n\n**Refresh tokens:** None are issued. The page says Intervals.icu \"doesn’t use refresh tokens, only access tokens.\"\n\n**Expiry:** The page does not document a token lifetime. A 2022 forum reply describes the token as effectively one-time, with a new login replacing the old token, but this is anecdotal. Another user reported 403 errors after a few hours, and no official answer appears in the thread. David also said a new token is generated on each authorization and replaces any existing one.\n\n**Redirect URI rules:**\n- Redirect URIs must be registered on the app's management page.\n- For registered `http://localhost` or `http://127.0.0.1` URIs, the port is ignored.\n- Public clients do not get the automatic localhost exception, so they must register the exact localhost URIs they use.\n\n**Other requirements:**\n- The app must be approved before the OAuth flow works. Until then it shows as \"Pending.\"\n- Declined consent returns `error=access_denied` to the redirect URI.\n- PKCE mismatches are rejected: a verifier without a challenge, or a challenge without a verifier.\n- Once \"Require PKCE\" is enabled, authorizations without a challenge are rejected.\n- To revoke a token, send a DELETE to `https://intervals.icu/api/v1/disconnect-app` with a Bearer header. This stops webhook delivery.\n\n**Reported invalid_request errors:** The page does not mention any `invalid_request` error. The only errors reported are `access_denied` (user declined) and a 403 reported by one developer, with no confirmed cause. The documented rejections above (PKCE mismatches and missing `client_secret`) are the closest to request-validation failures.","durationMs":9620,"url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014mz3w6ccJ1eYe3kmjvcZMn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
